{
  "@@locale": "en",

  "privacyPageTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyLastUpdated": "Last Updated: November 14, 2026",

  "privacyS1Title": "1. Introduction",
  "privacyS1P1": "NanoSolve Hive (\"App\", \"we\", \"our\", or \"us\") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, why, and who else handles it when you use the NanoSolve Hive app for iPhone and Android or the website web.nanosolve.org.",
  "privacyS1P2": "By using NanoSolve Hive, you agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with our privacy practices, please do not use our application.",

  "privacyS2Title": "2. Information We Collect",
  "privacyS2DeviceTitle": "Device Information",
  "privacyS2DeviceItems": "Device type, operating system and app version\nDevice language\nYour time zone, only when you save daily digest settings\nA push notification token from Apple or Google, only if you allow notifications",
  "privacyS2UsageTitle": "Usage Information",
  "privacyS2UsageItems": "Which screens you open and which buttons you press, so we can see where the app confuses people\nEach record carries a random installation number created on your device. It is not linked to you, your account, your email or your phone\nThese records are deleted after 180 days, and nothing is collected while usage statistics are turned off",
  "privacyS2AnalyticsTitle": "Crash Reports",
  "privacyS2AnalyticsItems": "When the app crashes, Firebase Crashlytics receives the error, the app version and the device's technical state at that moment\nCrash reports contain no email, nickname or ideas\nNo crash reports are sent while usage statistics are turned off",
  "privacyS2UserTitle": "Optional User-Provided Information",
  "privacyS2UserItems": "Display name/nickname (for the leaderboard)\nEmail address (for your profile, the daily digest and the emails you opt into)\nDaily digest preferences: keywords, delivery hour, time zone, and whether email and the monthly summary are on\nPapers you save to your Vault\nSolution ideas, attachments, and other contributions you submit",

  "privacyS3Title": "3. Submitted Ideas — Open License",
  "privacyS3HighlightLabel": "Short version:",
  "privacyS3Highlight": "You keep the copyright to your idea. By submitting, you license it openly under CC BY 4.0 — so any scientist, NGO, or government can use it to fight nanoplastic pollution. We credit you. No one can lock the idea away.",
  "privacyS3OwnerTitle": "You retain ownership",
  "privacyS3OwnerP": "All ideas, texts, and attachments you submit remain your intellectual property. NanoSolve Hive makes no claim to ownership of your contributions.",
  "privacyS3LicenseTitle": "License you grant",
  "privacyS3LicenseP": "By submitting a Contribution, you grant NanoSolve Hive and the public a worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable license under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) to use, share, adapt, and build upon your Contribution — including for scientific research, policy proposals, and environmental applications — provided attribution is given to your display name or nickname.",
  "privacyS3LicenseLinkText": "creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
  "privacyS3WhyTitle": "Why open?",
  "privacyS3WhyP": "Nanoplastic pollution is a global problem with no time for legal barriers. Open licensing means a solution submitted in one country can be studied, implemented, and built upon anywhere — the same way open-source software accelerates technology. Your idea compounds in value the more freely it spreads.",
  "privacyS3PatentsTitle": "Defensive patents",
  "privacyS3PatentsP": "For high-impact ideas, NanoSolve Hive may — with the submitter's explicit written consent — pursue a defensive patent. The sole purpose is to prevent industry actors from patenting the solution and suppressing it. Any such patent remains royalty-free for research and public-benefit use.",
  "privacyS3NeverTitle": "What we will never do",
  "privacyS3NeverItems": "Sell your idea for private commercial profit without your explicit consent\nMisrepresent your idea as our own\nRemove your attribution after publishing",
  "privacyS3AnonTitle": "Anonymous submissions",
  "privacyS3AnonP": "If you submit without a name, the CC BY 4.0 license still applies but no attribution is required or possible. You will not be able to claim authorship after the fact for anonymous submissions.",

  "privacyS3AiTitle": "AI scoring",
  "privacyS3AiP": "An idea you submit is stored by NanoSolve and read by people working on the project. It is also sent to an AI service, which may be outside your country, to be scored, and the score comes back into the app. Your nickname and email are attached only if you choose. To delete a submission, contact us with the code shown when you send it.",

  "privacyS4Title": "4. Daily Research Digest",
  "privacyS4Items": "The daily digest is off until you turn it on in the app under Settings → My Vault → Research Preferences. It needs your email address, which you confirm with a 6-digit code we send to it; the code also keeps anyone else from reading or changing your settings.\nTo deliver it we store your email, your keywords, the hour you chose, your time zone, whether digest email and the monthly summary are on, and your device's push token.\nWe also record which paper was sent to which profile, so you never get the same paper twice.\nPapers come from public scientific databases. Choosing one uses nothing about you except your keywords.\nPush notifications travel through Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google) and, on iPhone, the Apple Push Notification service. They receive the push token and the notification text (the paper's title and summary), not your email.\nDigest emails and the monthly summary are sent through Resend, an email delivery service, which receives your email address and the message.\nTo stop, switch the digest, email or monthly summary off in Research Preferences, or turn off notifications for NanoSolve Hive in your phone's settings.",

  "privacyS5Title": "5. How We Use Your Information",
  "privacyS5Items": "Deliver the Daily Digest: Send the papers, notifications and emails you opted into, at the hour you chose\nImprove the App: Maintain and enhance application functionality and features\nAnalyze Usage: Understand usage patterns to improve user experience\nDiagnose Issues: Identify and fix technical problems and bugs\nComply with Law: Meet legal obligations and regulatory requirements\nCommunity Features: Display your nickname and ideas on the public leaderboard (with your consent)",

  "privacyS6Title": "6. Data Storage and Security",
  "privacyS6Items": "We store only what the app needs: your profile (nickname and email), your digest preferences and Vault, and the ideas or attachments you submit.\nYour email is never shown publicly. Your nickname appears on the leaderboard only next to ideas you submit under it.\nData travels over encrypted HTTPS connections and is stored on our servers, with access limited to the people running NanoSolve.\nIdea content and associated metadata remain in anonymized form after removing personal identifiers.\nWe never sell personal data.",
  "privacyS6HighlightLabel": "Data Minimization:",
  "privacyS6Highlight": "We only collect information necessary to operate the application and provide the requested services. We do not collect information beyond what is needed.",

  "privacyS7Title": "7. Third-Party Services",
  "privacyS7Intro": "Our application uses the following third-party services, each with their own privacy policies:",
  "privacyS7FirebaseTitle": "Firebase (Google)",
  "privacyS7FirebaseItems": "Purpose: Crash reporting (Crashlytics) and push notification delivery (Cloud Messaging)\nData: Crash reports as described in section 2; push tokens and notification text\nControl: Turn off usage statistics in Settings → Privacy & Security to stop crash reports; turn off notifications to stop pushes",
  "privacyS7AppleTitle": "Apple",
  "privacyS7AppleP": "Purpose: App Store distribution and push notification delivery on iPhone (Apple Push Notification service)",
  "privacyS7PlayTitle": "Google Play Services",
  "privacyS7PlayP": "Purpose: App distribution and updates on Android",
  "privacyS7EmailTitle": "Resend",
  "privacyS7EmailP": "Purpose: Sends the digest emails and monthly summary you opt into. Receives your email address and the message",
  "privacyS7AiTitle": "AI services",
  "privacyS7AiP": "Purpose: Scoring the ideas you submit (see section 3) and summarizing public research papers for the digest. Summarizing papers involves no personal data",
  "privacyS7WebTitle": "Cloudflare and content delivery",
  "privacyS7WebP": "Our servers sit behind Cloudflare, which shields them from attacks and sees your IP address. On the website, Cloudflare Turnstile checks that an idea is submitted by a person. The website also loads fonts and code from Google (gstatic.com) and jsDelivr, which receive your IP address when your browser fetches them",
  "privacyS7Note": "Each service receives only what it needs for the job listed above. We never sell personal data.",

  "privacyS8Title": "8. Your Rights and Choices",
  "privacyS8AccessTitle": "Access Your Data",
  "privacyS8AccessP": "You have the right to request a copy of all personal data we hold about you.",
  "privacyS8CorrectTitle": "Correct Your Information",
  "privacyS8CorrectP": "You can update your profile information through the app's Settings → User Profile section at any time.",
  "privacyS8DeleteTitle": "Delete Your Data",
  "privacyS8DeleteP": "Settings → User Profile → Delete account erases your account from our servers (your email, digest preferences, push token and Vault) and then from this device. Ideas you submitted stay, without your name and email. If you have not confirmed your email on this device, the app first sends you a code, so nobody else can delete your account.",
  "privacyS8OptoutTitle": "Opt-Out of Analytics",
  "privacyS8OptoutP": "You can turn off usage statistics and crash reporting in Settings → Privacy & Security. This does not affect core app functionality.",
  "privacyS8ManageTitle": "Manage Communications",
  "privacyS8ManageP": "Turn the daily digest, digest email and monthly summary on or off at any time under Settings → My Vault → Research Preferences. You can also turn off notifications for NanoSolve Hive in your phone's settings.",

  "privacyS9Title": "9. Children's Privacy",
  "privacyS9P": "NanoSolve Hive is not intended for users under 13 years old. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we become aware that a child under 13 has provided us with personal information, we will delete such information and terminate the child's account.",

  "privacyS10Title": "10. Data Retention",
  "privacyS10Items": "Submitted Ideas: Retained indefinitely unless deleted by you\nUser Profile, digest preferences, push token and Vault: Retained while your profile exists; erased on request\nDigest delivery log: Retained while your profile exists, so the same paper is never sent twice\nUsage Statistics: Deleted after 180 days\nCrash Reports: Retained for 90 days by Firebase Crashlytics, then automatically deleted\nApp Settings: Stored locally on your device; deleted when you uninstall the app",

  "privacyS11Title": "11. International Data Transfers",
  "privacyS11P": "Your data may be transferred, stored, and processed in countries other than your country of residence. These countries may have different data protection laws. By using NanoSolve Hive, you consent to such transfers and processing.",

  "privacyS12Title": "12. Changes to This Privacy Policy",
  "privacyS12P1": "We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our practices, technology, legal requirements, or other factors. We will notify you of material changes by:",
  "privacyS12Items": "Posting the updated policy within the application\nUpdating the \"Last Updated\" date at the top of this page\nRequesting your consent if required by applicable law",
  "privacyS12P2": "Your continued use of the application following the posting of revised Privacy Policy means that you accept and agree to the changes.",

  "privacyS13Title": "13. California Privacy Rights (CCPA)",
  "privacyS13P": "If you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), including the right to know, delete, and opt-out of sales of your personal information. To exercise these rights, please contact us using the information below.",

  "privacyS14Title": "14. European Privacy Rights (GDPR)",
  "privacyS14P": "If you are in the European Union, you have rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), including the right to access, rectification, erasure, and data portability. You also have the right to object to processing and the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.",

  "privacyS15Title": "15. Contact Us",
  "privacyS15P1": "If you have privacy concerns, questions about this policy, or wish to exercise any of your rights, please contact us:",
  "privacyS15HighlightTeam": "NanoSolve Hive Privacy Team",
  "privacyS15HighlightEmail": "Email: support@nanosolve.org",
  "privacyS15HighlightContact": "Or use the \"Contact Us\" option in the app Settings → About section",
  "privacyS15P2": "We will respond to your request within 30 days.",
  "privacyS15P3": "When you ask us to delete your personal data, we will remove any identifying information tied to your account, but accept that ideas, contributions, or other anonymized content you previously submitted may remain in the database as part of aggregated analytics, as those entries no longer contain personal identifiers.",

